From: ARMDeck <noreply@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8250-oneplus-instantnoodle: match PM8009 camera rails to the OnePlus vendor DT

The Xo666 board DTS marks all seven PM8009 LDOs (the camera PMIC) as
regulator-always-on, but only two of them have a consumer here: L3F (front
camera IMX471 vdig) and L7F (camera I/O, front camera and its EEPROM).
L1F, L2F, L4F, L5F and L6F have no consumer at all.

In the OnePlus 8 vendor device tree (LineageOS/android_kernel_oneplus_sm8250,
arch/arm64/boot/dts/vendor/19821, 82 .dts/.dtsi files scanned) every PM8009
LDO is used only by camera modules: L1F/L3F/L4F as cam_vdig, L2F as
cam_v_custom2 of the rear main camera, L5F/L6F as cam_vaf (autofocus),
L7F as cam_vio. The camera driver powers them only while that camera is in
use. Rear cameras are not supported on this kernel, so forcing their rails
on just keeps unpowered-by-design hardware energized from boot.

L2F is also set to 1.2 V here, while the vendor DT runs it at exactly
1.1 V (camera/kona-oem-camera-instantnoodle.dtsi, rear "wide" sensor:
rgltr-min-voltage/rgltr-max-voltage 1100000 for cam_v_custom2, and
kona-regulators.dtsi: pm8009_l2 min=max=1100000). This was the only one of
37 RPMh regulators whose mainline limits exceed the vendor limits.

Changes:
- drop regulator-always-on from L1F, L2F, L4F, L5F, L6F
- L2F: 1.2 V -> 1.104 V (label kept to avoid touching anything else).
  L2F is a pmic5_nldo: 320 mV + n * 8 mV, so 1.100 V itself is not a
  valid setting. A first version of this patch asked for exactly
  1100000 uV; the regulator core could not set it, so the whole PM8009
  regulator device failed to probe (-ENOTRECOVERABLE), which also left the
  QCA6390 WiFi/BT power unit (fed by S2F) and the front camera without
  supplies. 1.104 V is the step the vendor driver rounds 1.1 V up to, and
  the value L1F already uses.
L3F and L7F are unchanged, so the front camera keeps its supplies.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-instantnoodle.dts	2026-10-01 19:52:43.772692982 +0300
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8250-oneplus-instantnoodle.dts	2026-10-01 19:52:43.803581677 +0300
@@ -808,15 +808,13 @@
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <1104000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <1104000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
-			regulator-always-on;
 		};
 
 		vreg_l2f_1p2: ldo2 {
 			regulator-name = "vreg_l2f_1p2";
-			regulator-min-microvolt = <1200000>;
-			regulator-max-microvolt = <1200000>;
+			regulator-min-microvolt = <1104000>;
+			regulator-max-microvolt = <1104000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
-			regulator-always-on;
 		};
 		
 		vreg_l3f_1p05: ldo3 {
@@ -832,7 +830,6 @@
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <1056000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <1056000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
-			regulator-always-on;
 		};
 
 		vreg_l5f_2p8: ldo5 {
@@ -840,7 +837,6 @@
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <2800000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <3000000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
-			regulator-always-on;
 		};
 
 		vreg_l6f_2p8: ldo6 {
@@ -848,7 +844,6 @@
 			regulator-min-microvolt = <2800000>;
 			regulator-max-microvolt = <2800000>;
 			regulator-initial-mode = <RPMH_REGULATOR_MODE_HPM>;
-			regulator-always-on;
 		};
 
 		vreg_l7f_1p8: ldo7 {
